# Everything in this repo ultimately executes inside a Linux container, so the
# working tree is normalised to LF on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows checks files out with CRLF by default. A shell script whose
# shebang ends in \r fails with "no such file or directory" — naming a file
# that is plainly there, which is a confusing afternoon rather than an obvious
# error. src/cmd/management-api/entrypoint.sh is copied into an Alpine image
# and is the one that bites first.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only artefacts keep their own convention.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
